## What the app stores on your device
Your best score, the highest level you reached, your chosen ball, and your sound and vibration settings. These stay on your device. We do not run a server and do not receive them.

## Game Center (optional)
If you are signed in to Apple Game Center, the app sends your score to Apple's Game Center so it can appear on the leaderboard. Apple's own policy applies to that data.

## Ads
The app shows one kind of ad: an optional rewarded ad, only if you choose to watch it after a loss. Ads are provided by Google AdMob. AdMob may collect and use data from your device, such as device identifiers, ad interactions, coarse location and diagnostics, to show and measure ads, and to prevent fraud. Where required (for example in the EEA and UK) the app asks for your consent first. See Google's policy: https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads

## What we do not do
We do not ask you to create an account. We do not collect your name, email, contacts or precise location. We do not sell your data.

## Children
The app is not directed at children under 13. Ads are limited to a general-audience content rating.

## Your choices
You can decline ad personalisation in the consent message where it appears, limit ad tracking in your device settings, or simply not watch the optional ad.

